Without an option, write the embedded roff source to standard output:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
tk manpage | man \-l \-
.fi
.RE
.PP
Installation writes the same bytes to
.IR <prefix>/share/man/man1/tk.1 ,
where the prefix is the parent of the running executable's directory.
It stages the file before replacement, preserving an existing manual if
installation fails. Windows skips installation with an informational message.
